        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.32,
          "end": 40.71,
          "en": "And this is how you can add additional constructor functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.71,
          "end": 41.883,
          "en": "to your classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.11,
          "end": 44.88,
          "en": "And this is of course a feature we used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.88,
          "end": 46.68,
          "en": "from time to time in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.68,
          "end": 50.07,
          "en": "For example, here on EdgeInsets.symmetric,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.07,
          "end": 52.68,
          "en": "where we create such a EdgeInsets object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 52.68,
          "end": 56.31,
          "en": "by using the alternative symmetric constructor function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.31,
          "end": 58.26,
          "en": "This here is how you can define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.26,
          "end": 60.78,
          "en": "your own alternative constructive functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 60.78,
          "end": 63.753,
          "en": "alternatives to the default constructive function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.1,
          "end": 68.25,
          "en": "So what's the idea behind this alternative then?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 68.25,
          "end": 70.08,
          "en": "Well, my idea here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 70.08,
          "end": 75.08,
          "en": "is that I do get a list of expenses here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.65,
          "end": 79.53,
          "en": "which could be named allExpenses here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.53,
          "end": 82.41,
          "en": "So this is simply a parameter accepted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.41,
          "end": 84.24,
          "en": "by this constructive function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 84.24,
          "end": 85.56,
          "en": "So we expect to get a list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 85.56,
          "end": 88.8,
          "en": "of all expenses here from all categories.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 88.8,
          "end": 91.51,
          "en": "And I also want get a second argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.18,
          "end": 95.1,
          "en": "which sets the category,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 95.1,
          "end": 98.1,
          "en": "which is one of the properties I do wanna set here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 98.1,
          "end": 101.52000000000001,
          "en": "And now the idea behind this extra constructor function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 101.52000000000001,
          "end": 104.64,
          "en": "is that we add some logic to this constructor function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.64,
          "end": 107.31,
          "en": "to go through all the expenses we got,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 107.31,
          "end": 110.64,
          "en": "and then filter out the ones that belong to this category",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 110.64,
          "end": 113.97,
          "en": "so that we can set the expenses for this ExpenseBucket,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 113.97,
          "end": 116.82,
          "en": "which is tied to one specific category",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 116.82,
          "end": 121.35,
          "en": "to a list of expenses that only are for that category.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 121.35,
          "end": 124.11,
          "en": "So this is simply a utility constructor function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 124.11,
          "end": 127.05,
          "en": "that takes care of filtering out the expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.05,
          "end": 129.033,
          "en": "that belong to a specific category.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 130.29,
          "end": 133.98,
          "en": "Now two said this expenses property to the expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 133.98,
          "end": 136.32,
          "en": "that have this category at the point of time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 136.32,
          "end": 138.15,
          "en": "this constructor function is called,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 138.15,
          "end": 140.91,
          "en": "we have to add a so-called initializer list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 140.91,
          "end": 142.02,
          "en": "by adding a colon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 142.02,
          "end": 145.17000000000002,
          "en": "after our constructor function parameters here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 145.17000000000002,
          "end": 147.303,
          "en": "so after this closing parenthesis,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 148.62,
          "end": 151.89,
          "en": "and then here you can set expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 151.89,
          "end": 156.703,
          "en": "So this property here equal to allExpenses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 158.07,
          "end": 160.92000000000002,
          "en": "so this list of expenses we're getting here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 160.92000000000002,
          "end": 164.7,
          "en": "and then filtered for the expenses with this category.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 164.7,
          "end": 168.483,
          "en": "And this can be done with help of the built in where method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 169.74,
          "end": 172.44,
          "en": "Now this is a method provided by Dart,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 172.44,
          "end": 174.54,
          "en": "which is available on all lists",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 174.54,
          "end": 176.49,
          "en": "and where is simply a method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 176.49,
          "end": 178.803,
          "en": "that allows you to filter a list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 179.7,
          "end": 182.55,
          "en": "It takes a function as an argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 182.55,
          "end": 185.49,
          "en": "so you pass a function here as an argument to where.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 185.49,
          "end": 189.273,
          "en": "Here, an anonymous function using this arrow notation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 190.62,
          "end": 192.69,
          "en": "And then you automatically get your",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 192.69,
          "end": 195.93,
          "en": "individual list items as input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 195.93,
          "end": 199.11,
          "en": "So here I get a single expense since this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 199.11,
          "end": 203.22,
          "en": "is executed on all the expense items in allExpenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 203.22,
          "end": 207.06,
          "en": "So every time it executes, I get one single expense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 207.06,
          "end": 210.09,
          "en": "And here we have to return true if we want to keep",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 210.09,
          "end": 212.19,
          "en": "that expense in the filtered list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 212.19,
          "end": 214.203,
          "en": "or false if we want to get rid of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 215.25,
          "end": 218.64,
          "en": "And here, of course, I don't wanna hard code true or false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 218.64,
          "end": 221.91,
          "en": "Instead, I wanna derive true or false dynamically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 221.91,
          "end": 223.32,
          "en": "by checking whether the expense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 223.32,
          "end": 228.21,
          "en": "I'm currently evaluating here has a category that's equal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 228.21,
          "end": 231.09,
          "en": "to this category here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 231.09,
          "end": 234.99,
          "en": "So to the category property of that class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 234.99,
          "end": 237.18,
          "en": "So if the expense I'm currently taking a look at",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 237.18,
          "end": 240.51,
          "en": "has the category I wanna set for this ExpenseBucket,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 240.51,
          "end": 243.42,
          "en": "I want to keep that expense in that list of expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 243.42,
          "end": 245.01,
          "en": "that is stored in this bucket,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 245.01,
          "end": 246.48,
          "en": "otherwise it should be dropped.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 246.48,
          "end": 247.98,
          "en": "That's what we're saying here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 249.3,
          "end": 250.65,
          "en": "And now we just have to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 250.65,
          "end": 253.11,
          "en": "that we convert this back to a list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 253.11,
          "end": 255.96,
          "en": "And here we have to check with a double equal sign",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 255.96,
          "end": 259.38,
          "en": "because a single equal sign tries to assign a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 259.38,
          "end": 261.33,
          "en": "which is not what we're doing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 261.33,
          "end": 263.94,
          "en": "With a double equal sign, we check for equality,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 263.94,
          "end": 265.83299999999997,
          "en": "which is what we want to do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 266.73,
          "end": 267.563,
          "en": "And with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 267.563,
          "end": 270.54,
          "en": "we got this utility constructor function in place,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 270.54,
          "end": 274.23,
          "en": "which we will soon use to create different buckets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 274.23,
          "end": 277.713,
          "en": "that are represented by chart bars in our chart.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
